cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this sandbox or the episodes dataset, please cite them as below."
title: "latent-agent-sandbox: a recreation of the pattern of agent shortcut incidents with mechanical labels and a per-step hold hook"
authors:
  - name: "Latent Systems, Inc."
contact:
  - name: "Latent Systems, Inc."
    email: "founders@runlatent.ai"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-22"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/runlatentai/latent-agent-sandbox"
url: "https://github.com/runlatentai/latent-agent-sandbox"
abstract: >-
  An offline Docker sandbox in which a coding agent works on graded tasks while a planted, harmless, forbidden
  resource (an answer key, a funded payment key, a shared scratchpad) is reachable with a listing or a read.
  Every episode is labeled mechanically from the sandbox's access logs (discovery step, first violating step,
  used result, concealment). A per-step monitor hook can hold a tool call before it runs. Nothing here recreates
  a real exploit or a real system; it is a recreation of the pattern of publicly reported incidents.
references:
  - type: data
    title: "latent-agent-sandbox-episodes: natural shortcut-taking and honest episodes of gpt-oss-120b in the sandbox, with access-log labels"
    authors:
      - name: "Latent Systems, Inc."
    version: 0.1.0
    date-released: "2026-10-22"
    license: CC-BY-4.0
    url: "https://huggingface.co/datasets/runlatent/latent-agent-sandbox-episodes"
    notes: "Released beside the sandbox; the transcripts contain a model reasoning about taking a planted shortcut, which is the point of the data, and no technique."
